DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The uuttiiccoomm driver supports serial port functionality on devices based on
     the Texas Instruments TUSB3410 serial to USB converter chip.

     The device is accessed through the ucom(4) driver which makes it behave
     like a tty(4).

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     intro(4), tty(4), ucom(4), uhub(4), usb(4)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The uuttiiccoomm device driver first appeared in OpenBSD 4.3.

AAUUTTHHOORRSS
     The uuttiiccoomm driver was written by Dmitry Komissaroff <_d_x_i_@_m_a_i_l_._r_u> and
     Hasso Tepper <_h_a_s_s_o_@_e_s_t_p_a_k_._e_e>.

CCAAVVEEAATTSS
     The uuttiiccoomm driver doesn't support devices that have an internal EEPROM
     with firmware, since such firmware is different to that supplied with
     OpenBSD.

     Devices with multiple ports will attach all ports, though only the first
     port can be used for now.

